WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.589
This query looks very similar to the previous one
but the meaning

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:08.938
changes because the glucose condition moved from ON
to WHERE The LEFT

00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:13.307
JOIN first preserves patients and creates
NULL-extended lab columns for patients with

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:17.599
no matching lab row Then WHERE asks whether the lab
test name

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:23.215
equals Glucose For unmatched patients the test name
is NULL

00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:29.677
That condition is not true so those rows are
filtered out Run

00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:33.904
this query and compare the row count with the
previous slide You

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:39.223
should see only patients who actually have glucose
tests This is a

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:44.107
common source of bugs because the SQL still runs
successfully There is

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:49.373
no syntax error to warn you A strong debugging
method is to

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.992
run both versions side by side and ask which
population the business

00:00:53.018 --> 00:00:58.876
question requires If the requirement says all
patients the previous ON-filter version

00:00:58.902 --> 00:01:00.271
is the appropriate pattern
